{
  "name": "Omnichannel Support Ticket Triage & Smart Escalation",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. OMNICHANNEL INTAKE\nA new support email (Gmail) or a chat-widget message (webhook) both normalize into the same ticket shape: channel, customer, message, received_at.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 608,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "6cc9467c-2834-4173-b3d3-e79ff486cc37",
      "name": "Note: ## 1. OMNICHANNEL IN",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1856,
        -16
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. KNOWLEDGE BASE MATCH\nThe message is embedded (native Embeddings OpenAI subnode) and searched against the company's policy/shipping/technical KB using the native Pinecone Vector Store node (Get Many mode). The top match's similarity score becomes the 'confidence' signal. Returns 0 matches safely if the index is empty, defaulting to low confidence (escalate).",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "6d88d527-c4ab-4cda-b5f0-d1f67183b4b0",
      "name": "Note: ## 2. KNOWLEDGE BASE",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1232,
        -16
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. SENTIMENT & INTENT\nA native Anthropic node separately classifies sentiment, frustration level (0-10), and flags cancellation threats or billing disputes — this is the second signal, independent of whether the KB has a good answer.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b2e5ccb0-9ce7-484b-9155-72e178c62f21",
      "name": "Note: ## 3. SENTIMENT & IN",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -752,
        -16
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. THE DECISION\nHigh KB confidence + neutral/positive sentiment + no threat flags → auto-resolve. Anything else → escalate, tagged urgent or normal based on frustration/threat signals. This is the core IP of the workflow.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "88d480d5-8f4a-4b77-a8f7-3ed1c28aa017",
      "name": "Note: ## 4. THE DECISION\nH",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -272,
        -16
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5A. AUTO-RESOLUTION\nDrafts a KB-grounded reply and sends it back on whatever channel the ticket came in on, then logs it as resolved.",
        "height": 484,
        "width": 1400,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "aa514639-2c70-4012-be48-af13f4776734",
      "name": "Note: ## 5A. AUTO-RESOLUTI",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        320,
        -304
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5B. SMART ESCALATION\nBuilds an enriched summary for the human agent (message, sentiment, why it was escalated, relevant KB snippets) and routes to an urgent or normal-priority channel so senior reps see VIP/angry customers first.",
        "height": 464,
        "width": 1192,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "5adfebbe-a3c5-477b-9a6e-4aa1585142db",
      "name": "Note: ## 5B. SMART ESCALAT",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        336,
        224
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ERROR HANDLING\nAny failure (KB search timeout, LLM error) fires this trigger and alerts ops instead of a customer getting silence.",
        "height": 308,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "72d64053-6b62-4564-b47d-6fae1b98aca9",
      "name": "Note: ## ERROR HANDLING\nAn",
